  "HelpBody": "Hover over a folder name in the address bar to highlight it, then click to navigate. For long paths, use the left … menu to choose a folder. Click empty space to edit the path; Esc cancels editing.\n\nCtrl + L / Alt + D: Edit the path, then Enter to navigate\nCtrl + Shift + C: Copy the current folder path\nAlt + ← / → / ↑: Go back, forward, or up\nCtrl + F: Search this folder\nF5: Refresh\nCtrl + Shift + N: Create a new folder\nCtrl + C / X / V: Copy, cut, or paste\nF2 / Delete: Rename or move to the Recycle Bin\n\nSupports local paths, network shares (UNC), and environment variables such as %USERPROFILE%.\nPaste a file path to open its folder and select the file. Search includes files and folders in all subfolders.\nExisting items are never overwritten. Copying or moving symbolic links and junctions is not supported.\n\nSearch this folder and subfolders by name · /file files only · /dir folders only",
